PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Round-0 split (majority A, minorities B/C) converged to near-unanimous A in round 1; round 2 shows complete unanimity on A with reinforced arguments. All colleagues agree residual light-vs-dark Cy5 difference after phenol→benzyl-alcohol swap arises solely from direct, nonspecific action of the unchanged thioxanthenone photosensitizer (417 nm absorption enabling background H-abstraction/energy/electron transfer). 

Strong evidence cited: (i) signal collapses dramatically yet remains strictly light-dependent; (ii) thioxanthenone is sole common 417 nm absorber; (iii) post-irradiation Cy5-azide step identical. 

Arguments eliminating competitors: B ruled out (requires absent phenolic OH); C eliminated (thermal/ground-state retro-[2+2] would label equally in dark controls and independent of para-substituent, contradicting observed light dependence and substituent sensitivity); D absent (no carbene precursor); E added after irradiation. No remaining disagreements or errors noted. Prior stance (A) fully reinforced; no new evidence favors alternatives. Key preserved facts: exact structures, 50 µM/5 µM concentrations, 2 mg/mL lysate, 10 min 417 nm irradiation, SDS-PAGE readout after click. Unresolved mechanistic detail (precise background reaction of excited thioxanthenone) does not affect answer choice.}

